  "strings": {
    "PassionCode for Enterprise | AI agent workplace for organizations | PassionCode.ai": "",
    "PassionCode.ai brings your organization into AI: a measured pilot, a workplace per role and agents on every employee’s machine, on open-source tools you own. Designed for 1 to 1000 people. PassionCode for Enterprise adds analytics on agents and processes, control and policy, and your cloud or ours.": "",
    "PassionCode for Enterprise — an AI agent workplace for your organization": "",
    "A measured pilot, a workplace per role, agents on every machine and people who verify their work. Built on open source, designed for 1 to 1000 people.": "",
    "PassionCode for Enterprise": "",
    "AI agent workplace for organizations": "",
    "Business process automation with AI agents": "",
    "Mobile app publishers, SaaS companies, marketing agencies, e-commerce, software studios": "",
    "Bringing an organization into AI: process mapping, a measured pilot, workplaces per role and agents on employees' machines on open-source PassionCode.ai tools, analytics on agents and processes, control and policy, hosting in your cloud or ours, and the commercial license where needed.": "",
    "What does it cost?": "",
    "The tools are free and open source. You pay for the work we do for you — mapping, building, hosting, support — and a commercial license where you need one. The proposal names the price after we understand the processes; there is no fixed package.": "",
    "Do we have to use your cloud?": "",
    "No. The workplace can run on your team's computers, in your own cloud account, or be hosted by PassionCode.ai. Your data and your model accounts stay yours either way.": "",
    "Which models and agents can we use?": "",
    "Any. The workplace is agent-agnostic: Claude Code, Kilo Code and Hermes Agent connect to Fabric today, Codex and Cline run inside it, more are planned, and any agent, MCP server or tool you already run becomes a Fabric-compatible service.": "",
    "Do the analytics watch our employees?": "",
    "No. Analytics are about agents and the outcomes of processes: what ran, what it cost, what was approved. Nothing is stealth, and what is measured is visible to the people it concerns.": "",
    "When do we need a commercial license?": "",
    "The tools are under the GNU AGPL-3.0. Internal use, and changes you publish under the same license, need nothing. A closed product that includes them, or a modified hosted service whose source you do not publish, needs a commercial license.": "",
