    "01 / BRINGING YOUR ORGANIZATION INTO AI": "",
    "From a pilot": "",
    "to agents on every machine": "",
    "The same path one person takes, at the size of your organization. Each step is measured before the next one starts, and each says whether it works today or is where we are building.": "",
    "One process, one agent workplace, measured against its own baseline: the hours, the cost and every action the agents took.": "",
    "Workplaces": "",
    "A workplace per role: its agents, the accounts they run on, what they may do, and one window to see them.": "",
    "Agents on every machine": "",
    "Agents reach the computers of the people who need them. Today we install them with your team; rolling them out and updating them from one place is the direction.": "",
    "People as the experts": "",
    "Employees become the human in the loop: they verify what agents prepare, and build agents of their own that spread through the organization.": "",
    "Designed for 1 to 1000 people.": "",
    "One person starts free from the": "",
    "guide": "",
    "; a team of ten gets a workplace per role; a department of a hundred gets a measured rollout; an organization of a thousand gets PassionCode for Enterprise.": "",
    "Read the vision": "",
    "02 / WHO IT IS FOR": "",
    "The same workplace,": "",
    "shaped to the work": "",
    "Agents take the repeatable part of a process — gathering, drafting, checking, reporting — and leave the decision to a person, with the evidence beside it.": "",
    "MOBILE APPS AND GAMES": "",
    "Publishers": "",
    "Release notes and store listings from merged work, in every locale": "",
    "Store screenshots and creatives produced and checked against the guidelines": "",
    "Review replies drafted daily, escalations routed to the right person": "",
    "Release checklists that do not ship until the evidence is green": "",
    "SAAS": "",
    "Product teams": "",
    "Support inbox triaged by importance, answers drafted under a reply policy": "",
    "Weekly product and revenue reports assembled from your own data": "",
    "Code review, QA runs and changelogs carried by agents, approved by engineers": "",
    "Onboarding emails and docs kept in step with each release": "",
    "MARKETING": "",
    "Agencies and in-house teams": "",
    "Ad creative variants from one brief, each with its source and cost": "",
    "Campaign reports per client, every number traced to the platform": "",
    "Content and SEO pages drafted to the brand voice, reviewed before publishing": "",
    "Several model accounts and clients kept apart with Switchboard": "",
    "E-COMMERCE": "",
    "Online stores": "",
    "Product descriptions and translations across the catalog": "",
    "Price and stock monitoring with alerts that name the change": "",
    "Customer questions answered from your policies, refunds left to people": "",
    "SOFTWARE STUDIOS": "",
    "Outsourcing and agencies": "",
    "One view of every client project: activity, findings and what is stale": "",
    "Agents on many accounts and repositories without credential sprawl": "",
    "Client reports generated from the work itself": "",
    "OPERATIONS": "",
    "Finance and back office": "",
    "Invoices, reconciliations and month-end checklists prepared for sign-off": "",
    "Recurring reports from spreadsheets and accounting exports": "",
    "Every agent action written down for audit": "",
    "03 / WHAT IT SAVES": "",
    "The estimate is arithmetic": "",
    "you can check": "",
    "Hours your team spends on the processes each month, times the share agents can plausibly take over, times what an hour costs you. The share is lower when work is already partly automated, because there is less manual effort left to remove.": "",
    "hours a week × 4.33": "",
    "share agents take": "",
    "loaded hourly cost": "",
    "Share agents can take over, by how the work runs today": "",
    "Today": "",
    "Share": "",
    "Mostly manual": "",
    "Scripts and integrations": "",
    "Chat assistants used ad hoc": "",
    "Agents already run parts of it": "",
    "Example:": "",
    "40 hours a week of mostly manual work at $50 an hour is 173 hours a month; agents taking 25–50% of it is 43–87 hours, or $2,150–4,350 a month.": "",
    "An estimate, not a promise. The pilot measures the real number against your own baseline before anything is rolled out.": "",
    "04 / HOW WE WORK": "",
    "Measured first,": "",
    "rolled out second": "",
    "Map": "",
    "A call to walk through the processes you named: who does what, how often, where the data lives and what must never be automated.": "",
    "One process, one agent workplace, measured against its own baseline. You see the hours, the cost and every action the agents took.": "",
    "Roll out": "",
    "A workplace per role: the agents, Fabric Dashboards to see them, Switchboard where agents need several accounts, Project Observatory across projects.": "",
    "Operate": "",
    "Your team runs it, or we run it for you. Updates, new agents and support as the processes change.": "",
    "05 / PASSIONCODE FOR ENTERPRISE": "",
    "that need integration": "",
    "PassionCode for Enterprise is the edition for organizations that need the workplace tied into how they already run. It is in development: pilots run on the open-source tools today, and the edition is offered on request.": "",
    "Which agents ran, on which processes, what they cost and what people approved, across every workplace.": "",
    "Control and policy": "",
    "What each agent may do, which accounts and data it may reach, and which releases may install, set once for the organization.": "",
    "Help employees automate": "",
    "People who know the work get help turning it into agents of their own, reviewed before they reach anyone else.": "",
    "Run it in your own cloud account or hosted by PassionCode.ai. The models run on your own provider accounts.": "",
    "TRUST": "",
